\section{Global Attractor and Stability Basins}

Let \(\Gamma\) denote the phase space of all admissible manifold states \(\mathcal{S}\).
The dynamics under \(\mathcal{E}\) define a flow
\[
\Phi_t : \Gamma \rightarrow \Gamma, \quad \Phi_t(\mathcal{S}_0) = \mathcal{S}(t).
\]

A global attractor \(\mathcal{A} \subset \Gamma\) satisfies:
\[
\lim_{t \to \infty} \text{dist}(\Phi_t(\mathcal{S}_0), \mathcal{A}) = 0
\]
for all initial states \(\mathcal{S}_0\) in a basin of attraction \(\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{A})\).

Phase-space volume contraction:
\[
\frac{d}{dt} \text{Vol}(\Phi_t(U)) < 0
\]
for any bounded set \(U \subset \Gamma\), indicating dissipative convergence toward \(\mathcal{A}\).